{
  "api": "openai",
  "from_version": "v0",
  "to_version": "v1.0.0",
  "summary": "This is a total rewrite from pre-v1 to v1.0.0 requiring explicit client instantiation via client = OpenAI() instead of global openai.api_key and moving all calls under client. Response objects are now pydantic models requiring attribute access and model.model_dump()/model_dump_json() instead of dict access, and list() methods now auto-paginate instead of explicit .auto_paging_iter(). Dozens of attributes were renamed (api_base to base_url, proxy to proxies, InvalidRequestError to BadRequestError, Image.create to images.generate, etc.) and legacy globals and helpers were removed including a* methods (use async client), requestssession/aiosession (now httpx), Deployment, Engine, and embeddings_utils. The library now auto-retries with backoff, provides proper types, and ships Weights and Biases CLI in its own package.",
